1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,072
This is a tour of Shapr, using one project the whole way through:

2
00:00:05,052 --> 00:00:09,330
Aurora, a campus energy app, and a database that won't connect.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,637
Double-tap Command and circle anything on screen.

4
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:24,459
Shapr reads the text on your Mac, then offers to add it, or ask about it.

5
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:31,104
Or highlight text and press Option C.

6
00:00:31,084 --> 00:00:33,373
Every capture keeps its source.

7
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:39,961
Open a file while you work, and Shapr offers to add it.

8
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:47,550
Capture the same thing twice, and it isn't saved twice.

9
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,262
Captures sort themselves into packs.

10
00:00:57,470 --> 00:01:01,195
Hold Option S for the wheel, and point at a pack to equip it.

11
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:05,971
The map shows what a pack holds, and what belongs together.

12
00:01:05,951 --> 00:01:07,858
It's worked out on your Mac.

13
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:24,043
Ask a question, and Shapr answers from your notes.

14
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:30,520
Each point cites its source.

15
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,576
Answers run on your Mac, or with Claude if you add your own key.

16
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:41,358
Ask about a screenshot, and the answer draws on the picture and your pack.

17
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:52,095
Or use the pack with what you're looking at.

18
00:01:52,075 --> 00:01:55,596
You see what Shapr picked, and you can leave anything out.

19
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:09,699
Hold Option V, and say what you want.

20
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:20,388
Not sure what to say? Ask, and Shapr shows you.

21
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:33,745
Shapr drafts from the pack, and only from the pack.

22
00:02:33,725 --> 00:02:36,691
Nothing is pasted until you press Insert.

23
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:39,485
Forms are filled with values from your notes.

24
00:02:39,465 --> 00:02:41,948
You check each one. You press Submit.

25
00:02:43,770 --> 00:02:46,441
It picks the right pack for who you're writing to,

26
00:02:46,421 --> 00:02:50,853
and it can borrow your voice from a style pack, without taking facts from it.

27
00:02:55,770 --> 00:03:00,243
Passwords and IDs come only from your Vault, unlocked with Touch ID.

28
00:03:00,223 --> 00:03:03,127
Consent boxes are never ticked for you.

29
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:15,478
Save progress, and Shapr drafts a checkpoint:

30
00:03:15,458 --> 00:03:20,108
your goal, your rules word for word, what you've tried, and what's next.

31
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:29,698
When a free AI runs out of messages, Shapr hands the chat to another one.

32
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:34,792
The handoff waits in the message box.

33
00:03:34,772 --> 00:03:36,908
You check it, and you send it.

34
00:03:39,770 --> 00:03:40,913
Resume in any tool.

35
00:03:40,893 --> 00:03:44,790
If something changed since you saved, Shapr tells you first.

36
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:58,128
Keep sources connected.

37
00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:00,926
Share on your terms.

38
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:05,416
Let your AI tools use what you've collected.

39
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:10,355
Share a pack as a live link.

40
00:04:10,335 --> 00:04:15,144
People who add it stay in sync, and anything private waits for your review.

41
00:04:18,670 --> 00:04:21,055
Everything from here is a concept.

42
00:04:23,470 --> 00:04:27,605
Next, we're designing Shapr to follow your workflow, with your permission.

43
00:04:27,585 --> 00:04:31,716
You choose which apps it can see, and what it's allowed to remember.

44
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:44,992
Instead of starting another conversation from zero,

45
00:04:44,972 --> 00:04:48,872
Lens brings what you already know to the spot where you're working.

46
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:54,728
Not an endless recording of your screen.

47
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:03,344
A compact working memory:

48
00:05:03,324 --> 00:05:06,582
your goal, what you've tried, and what comes next.

49
00:05:11,170 --> 00:05:13,389
And when a decision gets complicated,

50
00:05:13,369 --> 00:05:16,989
explore the alternatives, and the evidence behind them.

51
00:05:24,370 --> 00:05:25,679
You stay in control:

52
00:05:25,659 --> 00:05:29,738
pause the session, revoke an app, or delete what it remembered.

53
00:05:29,718 --> 00:05:32,517
Temporary details expire on their own.

54
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:41,850
And when you come back, you don't have to start over.

55
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:46,970
Shapr remembers the work, so you can focus on doing it.

56
00:05:47,670 --> 00:05:50,007
Shapr isn't about collecting everything.

57
00:05:49,987 --> 00:05:52,422
It's about remembering what matters.
